	(text "TSOP38238 bare part: pin 1 OUT, pin 2 GND, pin 3 VS\n(dome facing you, left to right).\nIR receivers and hall switch outputs are active-low.\nEnable INPUT_PULLUP on D6 for the DRV5032.\nLIS3MDL range: set +/-16 gauss so it does not\nsaturate when the ankles are close."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 111.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1a6db742-eb64-43b7-b49d-4bd2211d361d")
	)
	(text "Wiring notes\nAll logic is 3.3 V. Never put 5 V on a GPIO.\nIMU INT1 -> D5 (RTC GPIO) wakes the ESP32 from deep sleep.\nPower the IMU from the 3V pin in the final build: the Feather\n  cuts STEMMA QT power in deep sleep. A QT cable is fine for week-1 tests.\nI2C pull-ups are already on the Adafruit breakouts.\nPN2222A TO-92: flat side facing you, pins left to right = E B C.\nMotor flyback diode: banded end (cathode) to VBAT.\nPin choices are suggestions - any free GPIO 0-21 works."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 129.54 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "369c1431-22ec-41dc-8235-5f1cbd7a7b09")
	)
	(text "Haptic driver: VBAT -> motor -> PN2222A -> GND.\nD12 high = buzz."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 43.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f3e57f68-cdee-4937-9d2d-f47ee8bebe69")
	)
